# Deny everything, then re-admit only the files the Dockerfiles COPY.
#
# An allowlist rather than a denylist: it can only fail by being too strict,
# which surfaces immediately as a build error. A denylist fails silently and
# permissively — a new directory or secret lands in the build context and
# nothing complains.
#
# This context is shared by Dockerfile.keycloak, Dockerfile.nginx and
# Dockerfile.postgres, so the list below is the union of all three. The
# Dockerfile being built is read separately and does not need admitting.

*

# Dockerfile.keycloak
!keycloak-realm.json
!keycloak-export-loop.sh

# Dockerfile.nginx
!nginx.conf
!robots.txt

# Dockerfile.postgres
!1-init-keycloak-db.sh
